From: Flax Advisors <support@flaxadvisors.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hostiface: store drives from the OEM push

The push carries Systems[0].Storage[] -- one entry per storage subsystem --
with the drives nested inside each, one level deeper than Memory or Processors.
The normalizer walked past them, so nothing on the BMC ever saw the NVMe.

Flatten them into a single "drives" group.  Drive ids are unique across
subsystems (NVMe_Device0_NSID1), so the flattening cannot collide, and the
group goes through the same merge-not-replace path as the rest: a no-change
delta omits Storage entirely and must leave what we hold alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform integration]
---
 redfish-core/lib/flax_host_interface.hpp | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/redfish-core/lib/flax_host_interface.hpp b/redfish-core/lib/flax_host_interface.hpp
index 2f1b861..5883ca9 100644
--- a/redfish-core/lib/flax_host_interface.hpp
+++ b/redfish-core/lib/flax_host_interface.hpp
@@ -382,6 +382,33 @@ inline void flaxNormalizeOemInventory()
                    nullptr);
         writeGroup("processors",
                    sys.value("Processors", nlohmann::json::array()), nullptr);
+
+        // Drives are nested one level deeper than everything else: the payload
+        // carries Systems[0].Storage[] -- one entry per storage subsystem --
+        // and the drives hang off each of those.  Flatten them into a single
+        // group; a drive id is unique across subsystems (NVMe_Device0_NSID1).
+        nlohmann::json drives = nlohmann::json::array();
+        const auto& storage = sys.value("Storage", nlohmann::json::array());
+        if (storage.is_array())
+        {
+            for (const auto& subsystem : storage)
+            {
+                if (!subsystem.is_object())
+                {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                const auto& list =
+                    subsystem.value("Drives", nlohmann::json::array());
+                if (list.is_array())
+                {
+                    for (const auto& drive : list)
+                    {
+                        drives.push_back(drive);
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        writeGroup("drives", drives, "Id");
     }
 
     const auto& chassisList = payload["Chassis"];
